  "body": "If you have an app opened in multiple tabs, you want to prevent read/write accesses at the same time.\r\n\r\nI originally thought `opened` (with device) / `claimed` (with interface) can be used for this, but it can't, because it isn't shared between multiple tabs of the same app; also, it has a different meaning.\r\n\r\nThere should be something like `openedSomewhereElse`  /  `claimedSomewhereElse` there (with a less stupid name).\r\n\r\nI have made a bug report at chromium bug tracker but then I realized it's more spec issue than implementation issue, I guess.\r\n\r\nhttps://bugs.chromium.org/p/chromium/issues/detail?id=679180",
